1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 { For the knight on b1 to go to g3 } 6... b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 O-O { White wants to play d4 so he has to pawns in the center. To prepare this mostly h3 is played to prevent Bg4 } { [%cal Gd2d4,Gc8g4] } 9. h3 { [%cal Gc6a5,Gc8b7,Gf8e8,Gf6d7] } (9. d4 Bg4 10. Be3 Nxe4 { Blunder } 11. Bd5) 9... Nb8 { This knight retreat is starting the Breyer. He wants to answer d4 with Nd7 } { [%cal Gd2d4,Gb8d7] } 10. d4 Nbd7 11. Nbd2 Bb7 12. Bc2 Re8 (12... g6 { Preventing the knight from infiltrating }) 13. Nf1 Bf8 14. Ng3 { Preventing the knight from infiltrating } 14... g6 15. a4 c5 (15... Bg7 16. Bd3 c6) 16. d5 c4 { [%cal Gd7c5,Gc1g5] } 17. Bg5 { Provoking h6 } 17... h6 { [%cal Gd1d2,Ga1a3,Ge1a1] } 18. Be3 Nc5 19. Qd2 h5 20. Ra3 *


